The copied app-restart script is gone; Stado restarts the app it installs

This repository carried its own copy of a shell script that restarted the
installed app after a build, one of sixteen copies kept in the desktop
repositories. Restarting is now Stado's: stado product install and update
of a desktop surface restart the placed bundle when its app runs, and
stado product restart restarts a bundle placed any other way. Stado's own
builds of this app already turned the script's restart off. The build
script's restart step runs only when the copy is executable, so with the
copy deleted it is skipped; moving that step onto stado product restart
waits on the numeric-literal gate, which refuses any edit of the build
script for the numbers it already holds.

Repairs: "The bundle's restart script waits for the application to exit, with no limit" the repository kept its own copy of a restart script Stado's product restart owns; the copy is deleted

